  "body": "Direct-PR: operator request 2026-11-10, weekly report format (tooling only)\nClaim: cloud/weekly-opus\n\n### Problem\n- The operator wants a new slide order for the weekly deck (overview, KPIs, milestones M1–M5, one feature-card slide each for M1–M4, the daily app, M5, today), with the existing style kept and only light iOS-style touches.\n- The donuts were wrong (« M2 · 7 % 2/28 » when M2 is 28/28): `build.py` read the stale committed `tooling/roadmap/state.json` (`generated_at` 2026-11-02).\n\n### Change\n- `weekly/build.py`: the 10 slides (order in the README). The tracker is fetched first and the state is written to `OUTDIR/state.json`. `generate.py` reads it through the new `ROADMAP_STATE` env var, so the committed snapshot is never used or rewritten. `--state FILE` reuses a saved state and refuses one older than 6 h. Every slide calls the legacy app « l'app courante ».\n- `weekly/counts.py` (new, pure): the gap Total, the changelog rows, the CI cap (« 2 500+ »), the state age, the three daily groups (`beta-test finding`, which never includes the credit label; `[Legacy` titles; `origin: legacy-evolution`), and title shortening.\n- `weekly/progress.py`: the charts are drawn at 1:1 with text of 20 px or more. They are split into `charts` and `donuts` for the KPI slide.\n- `weekly/shot.js`: fails a slide that overflows the page or its box, has overlapping body blocks, has text under 20 px, or contains the word « legacy ».\n- `tooling/roadmap/README.md`: the slide order and the format and counting rules.\n- No `state.json` or `milestones.json` is committed. This is a Linux-only tooling change: no `App/` or `Packages/` file is touched.\n\n### Tests\n- `scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py` has a new `WeeklyCounts` class covering:\n  - the gap Total, read from `## Counts` only;\n  - the changelog row count;\n  - the CI-cap formatting;\n  - the stale-state refusal (`build.py --state` with a 2026-11-02 state exits non-zero);\n  - credit-label exclusion;\n  - « legacy » removal from titles;\n  - the version parse.\n- All 59 tests pass (`python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests`).\n- Render: `python3 tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py OUT --since 2026-11-03 && node tooling/roadmap/weekly/shot.js OUT` passes all 10 slides, and I checked each JPEG by eye.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFWFFoopv7MySBP5rF)_",
