   "body": "Adversarial review, round 1 (Fable, read-only sub-agent), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head e2df5aa\n\n1. **Medium** — `tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py` (`gather`: `'planned': len(G.rows)`; `slide_overview`; `slide_m5`: `rest`). LOT-176 (#416, closed *not planned*) is still counted and shown. Slide 1 says « 174 lots planifiés · 53 restants », while slides 3 and 9 total 173 lots with 52 left (4 + 24 + 24). Slide 9 lists « 176 Galerie HD » under « Aussi dans M5 · 2 » next to a hero that says 0/24. Fix: exclude not-planned lots from `planned` and from `rest` (the same filter as `per_ms`), and add a test.\n2. **Low** — `build.py` `slide_kpis` (`for _, v, t in tiles`), the slide 1 KPI strip, the slide 10 cells. These cards have no icon, although the brief asks for one per card; `slide_kpis` declares the icons and discards them. Fix: render them, or drop the dead data and state the exception in the README.\n3. **Low** — `tooling/roadmap/weekly/shot.js` `audit`. Horizontal overflow inside a card is not detected. Probe: a long `nowrap` pill on slide 7 runs over the next card and the slide reports `ok`. The README says the script checks overflow and overlap. Fix: compare `scrollWidth` with `clientWidth` on `.card` and `.hero`, and check child rects against the card.\n4. **Low** — `scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py`. Two mutations leave the suite green: `generate.py` ignoring `ROADMAP_STATE` (the data-bug fix itself), and `page()` without `no_legacy`. Fix: one subprocess test for each.\n5. **Detail** — `test_roadmap.py:515`. `WeeklyCounts` is defined after `unittest.main()`, so it is skipped when the file is run directly; CI uses discover, so it runs there.\n\n**Verified**\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests`: 137 tests pass.\n- Rendered with `--state` and `--since 2026-11-03`: `shot.js` reports 10/10 ok, and the worktree stays clean (no `state.json` or `milestones.json` rewritten).\n- Slides 1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 9 and 10 read by eye; slides 4, 5 and 6 only passed the checker.\n- Counts match the tracker: feedback 32/17, backport 20/2, `[Legacy` titles 4/0, 6 open PRs to `master`. The CI cap is real (`total_count` is 2500 for both the unfiltered and `status=success` queries); 216 failures, 321 cancellations.\n- Mutations of the gap scope, the CI cap, the credit label, the changelog rows and the stale-state check each turn a test red.\n- `shot.js` catches injected 19 px text, « legacy », and vertical overflow.\n- No pseudo found in the slides.\n- Not run: the default fetch path without `--state`.\n\nFixing all five in one commit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
