   "body": "Adversarial review, round 2 (Fable, read-only sub-agent), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 1ca8808\n\nRound-1 status: 1 fixed for the instance (planned 173, `Aussi dans M5 · 1`), 2 fixed but with a regression, 3 partly, 4 fixed, 5 fixed.\n\n1. **Medium (regression of the icon fix)** — `tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py:360` (`.ic.sm`, absolute) and `:603`. On slide 10 the « lignes de Swift » cell draws `98 869 +46 249` under its icon: the text ends at x=1509, the icon starts at 1479, a 30 px overlap. The gap is 6 px for `3 157 +1 423` (slide 10) and 7 px for `216 · 321` (slide 2), so the next digit overlaps there too. `shot.js` reports all 10 slides ok. Fix: reserve the icon's width in `.kpi b` and `.cell b` (padding-right, or the icon in the flow), and make `shot.js` fail when a `.ic` rectangle intersects a text rectangle of its card.\n\n2. **Low (class of round-1 finding 1)** — `build.py:521` (`left_card`), `:308` (`milestone_view`), `:437` (`card_pill`), `:587`. Only `planned` and M5 `rest` use `D['dropped']`. `sync_state` keeps a not-planned closure out of `closed`, so `G.done()` is false for it: an M1–M4 lot closed as not planned is listed and counted in « Reste à faire · N », can show as a lever, and keeps its feature card at « En cours » for ever, while the hero excludes it from the total. Fix: filter dropped lots once, in `ms_lots()` or a shared helper.\n\n3. **Low (L01)** — `scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py:573`. Restoring `'planned': len(G.rows)` and removing the `rest` filter leaves the 140 tests green: only `dropped_issues` is tested. Fix: extract the planned and rest computation into a pure function and test it.\n\n**Verified**: worktree at 1ca8808; `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests` (140 OK); `build.py --state … --since 2026-11-03` then `shot.js` (10 ok, exit 0); JPEGs 1, 2, 9, 10 viewed; Playwright probe measuring icon and text rectangles; three mutations (planned/rest stays green; `page()` without `no_legacy` and `generate.py` without `ROADMAP_STATE` both fail, as they should); tree clean after the build; worktree removed.\n\nFixing all three in one commit (round 3, the last).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
