   "body": "Adversarial review, round 3 (Fable, read-only sub-agent), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVE** — head 88cf976\n\nRound-2 findings:\n- **1 (Medium, icons over values): fixed.** The 10 JPEGs show no icon touching a value. The new `shot.js` check works: with long values injected and the `padding-right` rule removed, slide 2 fails with six `icon over text`; with the rule kept, it passes.\n- **2 (Low, dropped lots): fixed except one place**, see finding 1 below.\n- **3 (Low, pure tested function): fixed.** `counts.live_lots` exists and is tested.\n\nRemaining findings, neither blocking nor visible in today's deck:\n\n1. **Low** — `tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py:589` (`slide_m5`). The feature cards still list lots from `G.rows` unfiltered. Scenario: the issue of LOT-148 closed as not planned → slide 9 \"Navigation\" shows 5 lines including \"Défilement continu\" above a pill \"À faire · 4 lots\". Fix: build `lots` through `C.live_lots(…, G.rows, DROPPED)`, as `card_pill` does.\n2. **Detail** — `build.py:292` (`dependents`). A dropped lot is not done, so it still counts in \"débloque N\". Fix: iterate over live lots only.\n3. **Detail** — `scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py:578`. The test covers `live_lots` only; removing the filter from `card_pill`, `left_card` or `ms_lots` leaves the suite green.\n4. **Detail** — `build.py:594`. When every remaining M5 lot is listed, the \"Aussi dans M5 · 0\" card renders empty.\n\n**Verified**\n- Worktree at 88cf976; `python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts/tests`: 141 tests OK.\n- Deck rendered with the given state (generated 22:57 UTC) and `--since 2026-11-04`; `shot.js` reports 10/10 ok, and I looked at all 10 JPEGs.\n- Totals agree across slides 1, 2, 3, 6, 7 and 9: 173 planned, 121 done, M1–M5 at 40/40, 28/28, 39/43, 14/38, 0/24.\n- French throughout, \"l'app courante\", no \"legacy\" in the slides.\n- Probe with four lots simulated as not planned (LOT-148, 183, 100, 055): planned count, slides 2, 3, 6, 7 and the M5 \"rest\" card all follow; only slide 9's card list does not.\n- The PR does not touch `state.json` or `milestones.json`.\n- Not run: Python lint (ruff and pyflakes are not installed here).\n\nThe review cap (3 rounds) is reached, so I am leaving the approved head as it is. The four remaining items (one Low, three details) are left for a follow-up; none of them shows in today's deck, where LOT-176 is the only dropped lot.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
